# Health session architecture rules

Read `docs/architecture/HEALTH_SESSION_ARCHITECTURE.md` before changing health session code.

## Product positioning

- **Somo** = healthcare financial agent platform.
- **Somo Health** (consumer) = Safe VideoGPT for Healthcare → finance rails (P3+).
- **Kelly PA** = physician assistant in `health-*` rooms — education only, no diagnosis.
- **Kelly front desk** = B2B PSTN receptionist — separate product; do not merge prompts.

## Agent stack

- Consumer health agent = `kelly-pa-video-orchestrator.js` (Groq + LangChain optional).
- Turn spine = `health-turn-service.js` (DB transcript SSOT, queued turns).
- Do **not** wire commerce checkout, `kelly-rails`, `video-consult-graph`, or Pinecone **coding** RAG into `health-*` rooms.
- Derm answers use education RAG via `video-tool-registry` → `_runDermPatientQA` / `patient-education-client`.

## Phase 1 cost defaults

- Input: browser STT or typed text → `POST /api/health-session/:id/turn` (session token required).
- No Deepgram, Retell, or paid TTS in default path.
- Vision: snapshot-on-trigger; YOLO default; Anthropic behind `HEALTH_VISION_ANTHROPIC_ENABLED`.

## File size limits

- Keep new modules under ~400 lines. Split before growing monoliths.
- Do **not** add health logic to `server.js`, `database.js`, or `retell-websocket.js` — use dedicated services/routes.

## UI surfaces

- Consumer: `unified-dashboard/health-video-landing/` (`/health-video/`).
- Provider HUD `business/video-call.html` is **frozen** — extract patterns only, do not merge.

## Session changes

When altering session flow, DB schema, or auth — update `HEALTH_SESSION_ARCHITECTURE.md` in the same PR.

## Acceptance gates

Before closing a health coding session, run:

```bash
cd middleware-platform && npm run health:acceptance -- --offline
```

Use `--live` when Groq or derm RAG changed. SSOT: `docs/qa/HEALTH_ACCEPTANCE_CONTRACT.md`.
